# DEBT-0017: Ad-hoc Serialization of Evidence Bundles in Adversary Workspace Context

## Compromise
In Task B2.M (`runtime/orchestrator/__init__.py`), `_serialize_evidence()` manually constructs a dictionary structure for evidence items in the Adversary's context instead of using `kernel.evidence.Evidence.to_dict()`.

## Reason
Needed immediate materialization of human-readable evidence fields (claim ID, command, result, artifact hash) into CAS so the Adversary could inspect evidence details during live R4 self-hosting runs.

## Ideal Solution
Refactor `_serialize_evidence()` to serialize evidence bundles strictly via `kernel.evidence.Evidence` and formalize an `EvidenceBundle` schema in `kernel/evidence.py`.

## Repayment Conditions
Repay during Phase 3 when implementing live Court MCP evidence submission (R5).

## Priority
Low

## Estimated Impact
Potential schema drift between runtime serialized evidence dictionaries and canonical kernel `Evidence` objects if new fields are added to kernel types.
